      "analysis": "The invariant M is the actual colimit determined by the original tower. Necessity of finite generation uses surjectivity of the canonical integer-product map, a genuine enumeration of countable M and finite tensor support; the zero group is allowed. Finite torsion-free modules over the integers are made finite free, yielding the actual Hom(M-dual,-) representation. Category-level countable limits quantify over both countably many objects and arrows, and canonical comparisons are tied to actual cone projections. Both directions of all five conditions, preservation of every small limit in the affirmative case, and uniqueness of every representing object are proved. The additional finite-stage criterion is noncircular actual transition equations, independently shown equivalent by finite-basis lifting and eventual equality.",
