      "id": "S4",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "The rank-one tower uses arbitrary integer coefficients, including zeros and negative values. A complete alternative argument applies the already proved finite-stage criterion: a linear idempotent on Z is zero or identity; the first case forces a zero in every tail and the second forces all later coefficients to be units. The converse constructs the criterion in each branch. The signs theorem explicitly spells units as +1 or -1. Cofinal zeros annihilate every actual record and give a natural zero representation; eventual units give a true stage/invariant equivalence and Hom(Z,-). Both representing-object isomorphism classes are exhausted, and a nonzero tail with cofinal nonunits is excluded. The actual doubling tower disproves rank-one sufficiency.",
