      "analysis": "The doubling invariant is actually identified with the subgroup of Q consisting of z/2^n. Integer linearity alone forces every endomorphism to be scalar multiplication by its value at one; addition, identity and composition formulas give the full endomorphism ring. Clearing denominators and the prime-power divisor theorem prove precisely the signed integral power units, with arbitrary positive or negative exponent. These are transported through the complete natural transformation equivalence, with actual natural automorphisms constructed and all such automorphisms exhausted. The forbidden sequence is the genuine record [j,id_Z], valued 1/2^j. Every hypothetical source has one stage n; coordinate n+1 then forces the impossible integer equation 2z=1. This is the canonical product comparison, and the independently proved finite-limit theorem remains valid.",
